{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And he said to Joseph.</b> The Sages, z\"l, said: this is Ephraim. And the Rabbi Moses said: a reminder of this is that the letters of ויאמר are the same letters as אפרים by the exchange of vav and pei, since vav interchanges with pei in the alef-bet of א\"ת ב\"ש. And it implies that Joseph was not a regular presence with Jacob, as we find similarly: ״ויקרא לבנו ליוסף״. And I heard from the mouth of the Rabbi Samuel, z\"l, the reason: because Jacob feared he would ask him the matter — how he was brought down to Egypt — and he would tell him that his brothers sold him, and Jacob would curse them, and he would thereby destroy the entire world. For after all, Rachel his mother — he cursed her without knowledge, when he said ״עם אשר תמצא״ — and his curse was fulfilled and she died on the road to Efrat. Here, if he curses them with knowledge, all the more so."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "The acronym אז\"ל likely stands for אמרו ז\"ל ('the Sages, z\"l, said'); translated accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:16.650554168Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}